{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>And I will lead, etc.</b> And I am leading the blind on a way they do not know, for a blind person, if he were accustomed to the way, would walk on it without light, and I will make the darkness as though it were light for them, and crooked places to level ground. Some say that this is an allusion to Israel's return from Babylon."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 42, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:57:34.296200142Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}